# Proposed features recognized from lip_bore.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F1: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F1_Top Plane(z=15.0)

# F3: outer profile under top cap F1: vertical wall loop F3 F5 F6 F4, top at z=15.0, base at z=0.0, material inside the loop (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F3_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
feature F3_Profile ProfileBoss(z=15.0, extent=15.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 60.0
    60.0 60.0
    60.0 0.0
)

# F7: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; flat floor F9 -- a milled bore; mouth blend F2 absorbed -- extent runs to the virtual sharp corner (10.0), not the wall face's own top (7.0) (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# a flat floor is milled, not drilled -- a twist drill leaves a conical point, so no drill run is suggested
# break the lip with: run Form(tool=..., surface=F7_Bore)  [the tool must be a CornerRounder whose ground arc is R3.0 -- the pairing refusal reads the declared radius]
feature F7_Bore CylinderBore(dia=24.0, extent=10.0, x=30.0, y=30.0, edge_round=3.0)
